Description: tidy took the attribute type of <ol> (the numbering: 1, a, A, i, I) for a proprietary one in HTML5 and XHTML5: tidy_parse_string() and tidy_repair_string() of PHP warned about it, and with drop-proprietary-attributes dropped it, though HTML5 allows it again (tidy-html5 issue #1012)
Origin: upstream https://github.com/htacg/tidy-html5/commit/e411ad0d2582471fe0961900b2789ee8b5b9cc4c (05.01.2022, on the branch next, no release after 5.8.0), as Gentoo carries it (app-text/htmltidy files/htmltidy-5.8.0-ol_type.patch, bug 916074), -p0

--- src/attrdict.c
+++ src/attrdict.c
